for many the holidays mean time with  family some siblings here in clark  county though aren't so lucky they're  broken up into different foster homes  but today saint jude's ranch for  children helped bring them together for  an early christmas celebration victoria  saha was there she joins us live in  studio with more victoria  these siblings only get to see each  other a couple of times a year so they  do their best to make sure every  precious moment they have together  counts especially during the holidays  some of joshua hutron's siblings i love  you guys  he's now 18 years old but growing up he  was forced to raise them for a while my  mom was just always kind of  just putting the kids on the older civic  until child protective services got  involved the other two the youngest they  went to foster foster home i went to a  group home  holidays are tough when they're  separated which is why the event hosted  by saint jude's ranch for children is so  important lutron's siblings along with  75 other children were able to fill the  adventure dome at circus circus and just  focus on family time with rides and  presents events like this are good  because i get  and count down the days until they meet  again  i got a chance to speak with the ceo of  this program she says these kids already  go through so much and the holidays come  with a lot of stress she's just thankful  for the generous donations from the  community to make this event so special  sasha
 

